// AlertResolveSchema Request body for resolving an alert. The field set is a flat union across every alert type; `x-alert-action-fields` on this schema says which fields belong to which `action`. `required` means the request is rejected without that field; each `one_of` group means at least one of its members must be present; `optional` means read when present and never UNCONDITIONALLY required -- but an `optional` field can become required under a condition (`map_value_once`, for one, is required to map a blank value), and any such condition is stated in that entry's `note`. So a payload generated from the three lists alone can still be rejected: read the `note` before treating an `optional` field as safe to omit. A `note` key, where present, is human-readable prose about that action's runtime checks and is not machine-consumable. `client_side: true` marks an action the client performs itself (navigation); do not send it to this endpoint. Per-alert runtime checks narrow this further, so the alert's own `spec.actions` remains authoritative.
