// CompositeDryRunAutoEnableState Auto-enable intent lifecycle on a CompositeDryRunJob (qctl apply).
//
// A NULL column value means "no intent" — GUI-launched dry runs are
// untouched. The cmapper executor delivers a 'pending' intent at the
// dry run's terminal finish (composite_dry_run.py hook); apply voids
// stale intents group-wide so at most one is live per group. A manual
// enable of a revision voids the pending intents of the group's other
// revisions.
//
//   - pending: apply requested auto-enable; awaiting the dry run's
//     terminal state.
//   - enabled: the enable succeeded (or the revision was already enabled
//     by a concurrent manual enable — idempotent success).
//   - withheld: not enabled, for a recorded reason in auto_enable_detail
//     (enable-gate failure, dry run failed/stopped/superseded, or a newer
//     apply or a manual enable of another revision voided this intent).
//   - failed: unexpected exception during the enable attempt.
type CompositeDryRunAutoEnableState string

