// ReleaseBlockReason Why the §4.3 data-review release gate is (or is not) holding a row.
//
// The member order below IS the order both classifiers check, and that order
// is BEHAVIOR-DEFINING, not presentational: the partial-undo guard runs
// BEFORE the per-field ledger, so a row that is simultaneously mid-undo and
// cell-vetoed reports “mid_undo“ (and buckets awaiting_decision).
//
// “releasable“ is an explicit member, NOT an absent value: on the wire
// “release_block_reason = releasable“ means "the gate passes", while
// “None“ means "not computed on this request". On an already-released row
// “releasable“ means "nothing is blocking", NOT "ready to release" -- the
// client reads “status“ alongside it. There is deliberately no
// “already_released“ member.
//
// Not a Postgres enum -- it is derived, never stored. No migration.
type ReleaseBlockReason string

